# SCHLAR — PROMPT 9: SHARED SCHOOL MODULES & CROSS-ROLE INTEGRATION
## One Connected School Management System | Consistent Records | Coordinated Workflows | Professional UX

You are continuing development of SCHLAR, an existing school-management web and mobile frontend project.

Implement **Prompt 9: Shared School Modules and Cross-Role Integration**.

Prompts 1–8 have established the application foundation and role workspaces. Your responsibility now is to connect those workspaces through shared records, common services, consistent workflows, and synchronized frontend-demo data.

The goal is not to create more disconnected dashboards. The goal is to make SCHLAR operate as one coherent school-management application in which authorized users work with the same underlying school records and each role sees the information and actions appropriate to its responsibilities.

**Core SCHLAR principle: “Simple enough for a first-time user, powerful enough for a real school.”**

Keep the interface easy to navigate without stripping away features, permissions, or necessary operational detail.

