# 4. CONNECT STUDENTS, PARENTS, STAFF, CLASSES, AND SECTIONS

These are foundational records used throughout the school.

## 4.1 Student records

Ensure the same student record is used wherever applicable by:
- Admin.
- Vice Principal.
- Teacher.
- Parent mobile app.
- Accountant / Fee Manager.
- HR / Staff Manager, where staff-related student references are relevant.
- Librarian.
- Transport Manager.
- Receptionist / Front Office.
- Exam Coordinator.

Each role must see only the information and actions permitted to that role.

When an authorized user updates a student's permitted profile fields, all relevant screens should reflect the update.

Do not duplicate the student merely because a student appears in a library list, transport list, fee list, examination list, or attendance list.

## 4.2 Parent and guardian relationships

Maintain consistent parent-to-student relationships.

Support the existing model's relationship types and multiple guardians where applicable.

Verify that:
- A parent can view only the students linked to their authorized account or demo identity.
- The Parent mobile app uses existing student records.
- Parent contact information remains consistent across authorized modules.
- Changing a relationship does not accidentally expose one family's data to another.
- The receptionist can look up permitted parent information without receiving unrestricted access.
- A student can retain relevant historical references when a parent or guardian relationship changes.

Do not create a Parent web portal.

## 4.3 Staff and teacher records

Ensure teachers and staff are referenced consistently by their existing IDs.

Relevant modules include:
- Admin staff management.
- Vice Principal operations.
- Teacher workspace.
- HR / Staff Manager.
- Timetable assignments.
- Attendance.
- Examination duties, where supported.
- Reception appointments.
- Transport driver or attendant assignments, where applicable.

Editing a staff member's permitted profile details should update relevant directory and assignment views.

Do not overwrite HR-only fields when updating a teacher's teaching assignment.

Do not treat a staff profile, employment record, teacher assignment, and user account as interchangeable entities if the existing model distinguishes them.

## 4.4 Classes, sections, subjects, and academic years

Maintain consistent references for:
- Academic year.
- Term or semester, if supported.
- Class or grade.
- Section.
- Subject.
- Teacher assignment.
- Student enrolment.

Verify that modules use the same academic-year and class/section references.

Do not allow the attendance module, timetable, examination module, and student directory to display contradictory class or section labels for the same underlying assignment.

Where historical academic data must be retained, do not rewrite past records merely because the student advances to another class.

